      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T06:57:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have data showing how often a failed transfer succeeds on retry, so I can\u0027t justify the current retry count.\n\nAfter checking the EC I2C driver and PDC firmware, an I2C error does not always tell us whether the PDC has already accepted the write. Replaying the transfer is therefore not always safe.\n\nI\u0027ll remove the generic I2C transfer retries and use the existing error-recovery path on failure. I\u0027ll also add error log including the error code, command, state, and transfer phase.",
      "parentUuid": "c3cda64b_34404dff",
      "revId": "8dae8ec94a55b128e2c07f9b6bca8422a6a1129d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
